ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo: gpio77 is the USB ID input, not a regulator enable

Risk: LOW. Prerequisite for the USB host patch (0009).

The board file inherited an "ext_3p3v" fixed regulator on TLMM GPIO 77 from
the APQ8064 reference boards. On flo that pin is the micro-USB ID input:
  - board-flo-gpiomux.c, msm8064_sp_gpio_config[]: ".gpio = 77, /* APQ_USB_ID */",
    configured GPIOMUX_FUNC_GPIO, GPIOMUX_IN, no pull;
  - drivers/usb/otg/msm_otg.c: "#define APQ_OTG_ID_PIN 77",
    id_pin_irq_work_function() (low = host mode);
  - board-flo.c: "&apq8064_device_ext_3p3v_vreg" is commented out of the
    device lists and board-flo-gpiomux.c comments out
    apq8064_ext_regulator_configs.
The regulator has no consumer and is only "regulator-boot-on", so the
regulator core switches it off at late init and the SoC then drives the ID
line low as an output. Drop the node.
